# .vercelignore — what the SITE deploy must never upload.
#
# The Vercel project builds app/ (the marketing site) out of this same repo, which is also where the
# engine runs locally. A local `engine:run` writes its working set (jobs.json can exceed 100 MB) to the
# repo root, and Vercel rejects any file over 100 MB, so those artifacts must never be uploaded.
#
# These are all local engine artifacts. None of them is imported by app/, and none is needed to build
# or serve the site.
jobs.json
jobs.json.*
seen-jobs.json
embeddings.json
latest.json
stats.json
kpi.json
*.stale-*.bak

# scratch + local caches
scripts/.fit-cache.json
tsconfig.typecheck.tsbuildinfo

# the engine + server themselves: the site never imports them, and shipping them to a CDN host is
# both pointless weight and unnecessary surface.
research/
